{"seq":6,"ts":"2026-07-27T04:24:15.085935Z","kind":"plan","phase_id":"investigate","actor":"engine","source":null,"intent":null,"reasoning":"Investigating CHG-1/v4.12.0 (commit abc123 taxcalc bump) as prime cause of payments-api 5xx. Proposing code NPE hypothesis vs DB rival; pulling error signatures, commit diff/blame, and service/DB metrics to confirm or refute.","delta":null,"action":null,"observation":null,"decision":null,"available":["enumerate_changes","propose_hypotheses","correlate_timeline","fetch_logs","fetch_metrics","fetch_traces","read_diff","blame","query_change_log"],"plan_calls":["error_signature_topk","search_errors","fetch_logs","get_commit","read_diff","blame","get_pr_for_commit","fetch_metrics","fetch_metrics","range_query"],"plan_ops":["ProposeHypothesis","ProposeHypothesis"],"todos":[{"objective":"Propose leading code-defect hypothesis and DB rival","calls":[],"ops":["ProposeHypothesis","ProposeHypothesis"],"status":"pending"},{"objective":"Fetch error signatures and logs tying NPE to TaxCalculator at onset","calls":["error_signature_topk","search_errors","fetch_logs"],"ops":[],"status":"pending"},{"objective":"Read commit diff and blame for taxcalc/TaxCalculator defect","calls":["get_commit","read_diff","blame","get_pr_for_commit"],"ops":[],"status":"pending"},{"objective":"Fetch service RED and DB pool metrics to challenge DB rival","calls":["fetch_metrics","fetch_metrics","range_query"],"ops":[],"status":"pending"}],"todo":null,"refs":{}}
{"seq":6,"ts":"2026-07-27T04:24:15.085983Z","kind":"llm_exchange","phase_id":"investigate","actor":"engine","source":null,"intent":"xai/grok-4.5","reasoning":"xai/grok-4.5 · 10314/1416 tok · 24606.27ms · 4 to-dos","delta":null,"action":{"model":"xai/grok-4.5","system":"You are a senior SRE running a disciplined root-cause investigation of a production incident.\nA deterministic engine drives you ONE phase at a time. Each turn you: (1) gather evidence by\ncalling tools, (2) mutate the incident graph ONLY through the closed typed-op grammar,\n(3) maintain ranked, evidence-backed hypotheses, and (4) return a verdict that routes the\nengine. You reason like a differential diagnostician: change-first, actively try to REFUTE\nyour leading hypothesis and rule OUT rivals — confirmation is Popperian, not vibes.\n\nHARD RULES\n- Use ONLY node/edge types and intents from the provided grammar/tool list. Inventing a\n  label, an illegal edge pair, or an unknown tool wastes the turn (it is rejected).\n- SIX DATUM CATEGORIES, one atom (`add_assertion`), one question. Set `species` by asking ONLY\n  \"what is this datum's temporal EXTENT?\":\n    · a write-once KEY that MAKES the entity what it is -> identity\n    · a timeless fact ABOUT it you never slice as-of-a-time (incl. renderable CONTENT: a diff,\n      a blame line, a distribution) -> property\n    · a value TRUE over a window you WILL slice as-of-T (a status, a version, a count, a severity)\n      -> state (valid_from; valid_to=null = still true)\n    · a measured NUMBER qualified by a stat+window -> reading (append-only, NEVER superseded)\n    · a point thing that HAPPENED, frozen at an instant -> event (occurred_at; retract-not-supersede)\n    · a bounded HAPPENING with start/end/outcome a subject PARTICIPATES in, maybe still open ->\n      span (started_at/ended_at; subject may be a NODE or an EDGE; the engine sets its phase)\n  TIE-BREAK property-vs-state: choose STATE (a window you never query is free; a missing one destroys\n  as-of-onset reconstruction). The NODE TYPES catalog lists each predicate UNDER its category, so you\n  never have to guess which species a known predicate is.\n- NEVER inline a raw high-volume stream. Author the judgment-granularity UNIT plus a HANDLE — one\n  rule, three ways: a metric -> a summary READING + a metric_query handle; a log -> a promoted EVENT\n  (or an error_signature) + a log_link; a trace -> a SPAN datum + its trace_id (correlation_id). The\n  engine fetches the curve live; the graph holds only the units you extract.\n- Graph structure (services, changes, commits, databases, segments, metrics, error signatures)\n  comes from TOOL CALLS — prefer `calls`. Emit direct graph `ops` only for: (a) the Anomaly\n  symptom node + its onset_value/severity_score facts in FRAME (and, in VERIFY, the recovery\n  fact `degraded=false` on the SERVICE — the Anomaly takes ONLY onset_value/severity_score,\n  never `degraded`), (b) hypotheses (propose/update), (c) no_evidence null results. Do NOT\n  hand-fabricate a service/db/commit/segment/change/error node a tool returns.\n- NEVER emit `add_edge`. Every structural edge (depends_on, connects_to, ...) comes from a tool\n  and every causal/evidence edge (caused_by, supports, refutes) is DERIVED by the engine from\n  your hypothesis's root_candidate + supporting/refuting basis. A hand-authored edge is rejected\n  and wastes the turn — encode causation in the hypothesis, not an edge.\n- LINK a datum to a hypothesis by CITING its id in the hypothesis `supporting`/`refuting` — an id of\n  ANY species (a state/reading fact OR an event/span), copied from the graph, never prose. The\n  interval-overlap IS the evidence: a SPAN whose window CONTAINS onset (a vendor outage, a change\n  window, a rollout) is `supporting`; a SPAN that does NOT overlap onset (ended before / started\n  after) is `refuting`. A span with a lost close reads ABANDONED (the query surface tells you which)\n  — never over-link a dropped close as a live outage covering onset.\n- Only emit `add_fact` on the Anomaly (onset_value/severity_score) or a Service (red_errors,\n  red_latency_p50, red_latency_p99, degraded). All other facts (pool util, retransmits, diff\n  lines, blame, error counts) come from the tools — never author them by hand (a fact whose\n  predicate is illegal for the node, or whose subject you mis-copied, is rejected).\n- IN FRAME you MUST, in the SAME turn, (1) call the change/alert tools that are wired for this\n  incident, AND (2) emit `add_node` for the Anomaly PLUS at least one `add_fact` onset_value on\n  it (the wired alert/change tools return nodes+events but NO facts, so the gate's min_facts is\n  satisfied ONLY by your Anomaly onset fact). Anomaly onset facts are the symptom you framed;\n  their exact value is your best read of the alert.\n- A tool's data lands in the graph you see on your NEXT turn — so read the CURRENT GRAPH\n  slice carefully; it holds the evidence from everything you called before.\n- root_candidate of a hypothesis MUST be a node id copied from the graph slice (the\n  initiating change/commit/segment/db), never prose.\n- A hypothesis `hid` is a SHORT local id like \"h1\"/\"h2\" (NOT \"hyp:h1\"). The graph shows a\n  hypothesis node as \"hyp:h1\" — to update it, pass hid \"h1\". Refute a rival by updating its\n  hid with new_status \"refuted\"; do NOT re-propose it under a new id.\n- The `root_candidate` is the ROOT (the initiating change/commit/segment/fault) — trace the\n  causal chain back to what INITIATED it, not the intermediate mechanism/resource it saturates\n  along the way. A saturated resource is often a symptom of an upstream change, not the root.\n  GENERAL PRINCIPLE — root at the ACTIONABLE CAUSE you would revert or fix (a change, a commit,\n  a config, a security policy/rule, or the load that saturates a limit). NEVER root at a resource\n  that is merely the CONDUIT the traffic passes through or the SYMPTOM it shows: if a resource on\n  the path is itself HEALTHY, it is a conduit, not the root. Ask \"what is the ONE thing I would\n  change to fix this?\" — that is the root.\n  Rooting convention by fault class: an application code defect roots at the CODE_COMMIT the\n  error/blame resolves to (the deploy that shipped it is the vehicle, not the root); a schema/\n  index/DB-migration or config change roots at the CHANGE_EVENT that made it (NOT the database\n  whose pool it later saturates — the pool is the mechanism); a TRANSPORT fault — the link ITSELF\n  is degraded (packet_loss > 0, retransmits climbing) — roots at the NETWORK_SEGMENT; but a\n  FIREWALL / SECURITY-POLICY block — the link is HEALTHY (packet_loss ~ 0, no retransmits) yet\n  traffic is cleanly DENIED — roots at the POLICY CHANGE that tightened it (or the FIREWALL_RULE\n  it modified), NEVER the healthy segment the denied traffic merely crosses. Distinguish the two\n  by the link's health: degraded link → segment; clean denials on a healthy link → the policy.\n  A fault GATED BEHIND A FEATURE FLAG — the defective branch was dormant until a flag flip\n  enabled it (error first_seen AT the flip; the commit that shipped the branch predates it,\n  often by days) — roots at the FEATURE_FLAG (the actionable revert is flipping it OFF; the\n  old commit is the mechanism the flip armed, and the flip's change ticket is the vehicle).\n  A LIFECYCLE EXPIRY — a certificate/credential lapses (days_to_expiry hits 0, handshake\n  errors first_seen at the expiry instant, NO change in the window) — roots at the\n  CERTIFICATE itself (the fix is renewal/rotation).\n  Copy that node's exact id from the graph as root_candidate.\n- Advance only when the phase's GATE is satisfied. In investigate you must reach a\n  high-confidence leader AND have ruled out a rival (or challenged the leader). A leader is\n  HIGH confidence once the root resource shows the fault DIRECTLY (the blame line on the commit,\n  the DROP INDEX in the diff, the retransmits/packet-loss on the segment, the saturation on the\n  host) AND the rival is ruled out — you do NOT need a separate change ticket to confirm. When\n  you have that, set the leader to status \"supported\" at \"high\" and ADVANCE; do not keep\n  re-investigating for more corroboration (repeating the same query is a wasted turn).\n- In verify, once the symptom has cleared, set the leader status \"confirmed\" and emit verdict\n  `advance` (the engine routes verify -> close); reserve verdict `done` for the CLOSE phase only.\n- The phase's `allowed_intents` are ABSTRACT CATEGORIES, not tool names. Always call CONCRETE\n  tools from the AVAILABLE TOOLS list. If a set of calls added NO new nodes/facts to the graph\n  last turn, that tool was not wired for this incident — switch to a DIFFERENT wired tool; never\n  repeat a call that returned nothing.\n- INVESTIGATE is ONE loop: hypothesize ⇄ gather evidence ⇄ refute. Early in the loop propose\n  the leading hypothesis AND at least one distinct RIVAL rooted at a different node; then\n  actively gather evidence that could REFUTE a hypothesis and set the loser's status to\n  \"refuted\" — the gate will not let you advance until a rival is ruled out (or the leader is\n  challenged with refuting evidence). Do not loop re-supporting one idea.\n\nOUTPUT: a single JSON object, no markdown, exactly:\n{\n  \"reasoning\": \"your differential reasoning for THIS phase (2-5 sentences)\",\n  \"calls\": [{\"intent\": \"<tool intent>\", \"params\": {}}],\n  \"ops\": [\n    {\"op\":\"add_node\",\"type\":\"<node type>\",\"props\":{\"<id key>\":\"<id value>\"}},\n    {\"op\":\"add_assertion\",\"subject\":\"<node id>\",\"name\":\"<predicate>\",\"value\":<value>,\"unit\":\"<unit>\",\"species\":\"state\",\"source\":\"<source>\",\"at\":\"2026-07-19T14:05:00+00:00\"},\n    {\"op\":\"add_assertion\",\"subject\":\"<node id>\",\"name\":\"<event type>\",\"species\":\"event\",\"source\":\"<source>\",\"at\":\"2026-07-19T14:50:00+00:00\"},\n    {\"op\":\"add_assertion\",\"subject\":\"<node OR edge id>\",\"name\":\"<span name>\",\"species\":\"span\",\"started_at\":\"2026-07-19T10:00:00+00:00\",\"ended_at\":\"2026-07-19T10:05:00+00:00\",\"correlation_id\":\"<trace_id>\",\"source\":\"<source>\"},\n    {\"op\":\"propose_hypothesis\",\"hid\":\"h1\",\"statement\":\"...\",\"root_candidate\":\"<node id>\",\"confidence_level\":\"med\"},\n    {\"op\":\"update_hypothesis\",\"hid\":\"h2\",\"new_status\":\"refuted\",\"basis\":\"...\",\"add_refuting\":[]},\n    {\"op\":\"no_evidence\",\"intent\":\"<tool intent>\",\"scope\":\"<node id>\",\"basis\":\"...\",\"at\":\"2026-07-19T14:20:00+00:00\"}\n  ],\n  (add_assertion is the atom: species one of identity|property|state|reading|event|span. A span's\n   subject may be a NODE or an EDGE; started_at/ended_at bound it (ended_at null = still open) and\n   the engine sets its phase — never author it. The ergonomic add_fact/add_event shorthand is also\n   accepted and folded to add_assertion.)\n  \"todos\": [\n    {\"objective\":\"<short aim for this step>\",\n     \"calls\":[{\"intent\":\"<tool intent>\",\"params\":{}}],\n     \"ops\":[ /* the SAME typed ops as above that serve THIS objective */ ]}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"concise phase narrative for the journal\",\n  \"verdict\": {\"status\":\"advance|repeat|backtrack|blocked|done\",\"confidence_level\":\"low|med|high\",\"basis\":\"why this verdict\"},\n  \"next_actions\": [\"what the next phase should do\"]\n}\nGroup your plan into a CHECKLIST of `todos`: each a short `objective` with the `calls`+`ops` that\nserve it, so the plan reads as to-dos executing one by one. When you emit `todos`, the engine reads\ncalls/ops FROM them — do NOT also fill the top-level calls/ops. `todos` is OPTIONAL: a flat\ncalls/ops with no todos still works — it becomes one to-do. Keep it lightweight — one objective per\ngenuine step; do not over-split.\nvalid op kinds: add_node, add_assertion, add_edge, propose_hypothesis, update_hypothesis, no_evidence, retract, merge, retype, reify.\n(`retract` tombstones a WRONG fact/event you previously folded — {\"op\":\"retract\",\"target\":\"<fact/event/edge id>\",\"reason\":\"...\"}; use it only for observations proven wrong, never to hide refuting evidence.)\nvalid sources: prometheus, splunk, appd, servicenow, cmdb, ocp, artifactory, git, bigpanda, llm, human, engine.\nvalid hypothesis statuses: proposed, investigating, supported, confirmed, refuted, superseded.","prompt":"# INVESTIGATION GRAMMAR (closed vocabulary — you may ONLY use members below)\n\n## NODE TYPES  (pick a member; never invent a label; `generic_ci` is the sole escape hatch)\n##   Each type declares its predicates BY CATEGORY — property / state / reading / span / event.\n##   The category tells you which `species` to author (§8.1 router): property=timeless fact ABOUT\n##   it (never sliced as-of-T), state=a value TRUE over a window you WILL slice as-of-T, reading=a\n##   measured number (stat+window), span=a bounded happening it PARTICIPATES in, event=an instant.\n  api_endpoint [L0]  id_keys=(service_name,env,method,route_template)\n     property=[status_code_dist]  reading=[error_rate,latency_p99,request_rate]  span=[hop]  event=[5xx_spike,timeout_burst]\n     - A specific method+route_template on a Service, carrying finer-grained RED than the Serv...\n  application [L0]  id_keys=(name)\n     event=[decommissioned]\n     - A business/product grouping that OWNS one or more Services; it is never itself deployed...\n  component [L0]  id_keys=(service_name,env,component_name)\n     event=[exception_raised]\n     - An internal module of a Service with no independent Deployment/Pod of its own\n  service [L0]  id_keys=(service_name,env)\n     state=[degraded,slo_availability_target,slo_freshness_target,slo_latency_target,tier]  reading=[error_rate,latency_p50,latency_p99,request_rate,request_rate_x_baseline]  span=[hop,trace]  event=[alert_fired,degraded_cleared,degraded_started,deployed,scaled,trace_captured]\n     - An independently deployable unit with its own Deployment, ApiEndpoints, and RED metrics\n  team [L0]  id_keys=(team_name)\n     (peripheral — no cataloged predicates)\n     - The human/organizational owner, referenced via OWNS/MEMBER_OF edges; never itself a run...\n  batch_job [L1]  id_keys=(job_name,schedule_id)\n     property=[last_duration]  reading=[backlog_size]  event=[completed,failed,skipped,started]\n     - A scheduled/triggered unit of work with a bounded start/end (cron or event-triggered), ...\n  container [L1]  id_keys=(pod_uid,container_name)\n     state=[image]  event=[OOMKilled,restarted,started,terminated]\n     - A single container within a Pod, for per-container facts finer-grained than the Pod agg...\n  deployment [L1]  id_keys=(uid)\n     state=[available_replicas,desired_replicas,image,rollout_progress]  event=[image_change,rollback,rollout_complete,rollout_started]\n     - The desired-state controller owning a Service's ReplicaSets/Pods\n  pod [L1]  id_keys=(uid)\n     property=[node_name]  state=[image,phase,ready]  reading=[cpu_utilization,mem_utilization,restart_count]  event=[OOMKilled,evicted,restarted,scheduled,started,terminated]\n     - A running instance realizing a ReplicaSet, scheduled onto exactly one Host via RUNS_ON\n  process [L1]  id_keys=(host_ref,process_name)\n     event=[crashed,restarted,started]\n     - A bare OS process on a Host with no Pod/Container orchestration above it\n  replicaset [L1]  id_keys=(uid)\n     event=[scaled]\n     - A generation/revision snapshot owned by a Deployment\n  cluster [L2]  id_keys=(cluster_id)\n     event=[degraded,upgraded]\n     - The top-level orchestration platform (e.g\n  config_item [L2]  id_keys=(ci_id)\n     event=[attribute_changed]\n     - The generic CMDB CI shape for a platform/infra item with no more specific typed NodeTyp...\n  host [L2]  id_keys=(fqdn)\n     reading=[cpu_saturation,cpu_utilization,disk_saturation,disk_utilization,mem_utilization,net_utilization]  event=[NotReady,disk_fail,reboot,recovered]\n     - A physical/virtual machine — USE metrics (util+saturation) attach here\n  namespace [L2]  id_keys=(cluster_ref,name)\n     event=[created,quota_exceeded]\n     - A logical partition within a Cluster grouping Deployments/Pods; workloads relate to it ...\n  cache [L3]  id_keys=(cache_id)\n     reading=[eviction_rate,hit_rate,mem_utilization]  event=[failover,flushed]\n     - An in-memory cache/store (Redis/Memcached-like) a Service reads/writes for low-latency ...\n  database [L3]  id_keys=(db_id)\n     state=[max_connections]  reading=[active_connections,conn_pool_util,replication_lag,slow_query_rate]  event=[connection_storm,deadlock_spike,failover,migration_applied]\n     - A database instance/cluster — instance-level facts (pool, replication, failover) attach...\n  message_queue [L3]  id_keys=(topic_id)\n     reading=[consumer_lag,dlq_depth,throughput]  event=[partition_offline,rebalance]\n     - An async messaging topic/queue\n  schema [L3]  id_keys=(db_id,schema_name)\n     property=[index_health,table_count]  event=[index_dropped,migration_applied]\n     - A named schema/table-group inside a Database — used when a change (migration, dropped i...\n  api_gateway [L4]  id_keys=(gateway_id)\n     event=[auth_reject_spike,config_deployed,rate_limit_tripped,route_remapped]\n     - An API gateway (Kong/Apigee/AWS-APIGW/Istio-GW/APIM) owning auth, rate-limit, quota and...\n  cdn [L4]  id_keys=(cdn_id)\n     event=[cache_purged,config_deployed,origin_fetch_error,pop_outage]\n     - A content delivery network (CloudFront/Akamai/Fastly/Cloudflare) — the outermost path-d...\n  dns [L4]  id_keys=(record_name,record_type)\n     event=[record_changed]\n     - A DNS record resolving a name to a target — the naming family — use when a symptom trac...\n  firewall_rule [L4]  id_keys=(rule_id)\n     reading=[deny_count]  event=[deny_spike,rule_changed]\n     - A specific ACL/policy rule; the protected resource points at it via SECURED_BY\n  load_balancer [L4]  id_keys=(lb_id)\n     event=[backend_marked_down,backend_marked_up,config_changed]\n     - Routes traffic to Service backends via ROUTES_TO; distinguishes from Route (a single ru...\n  network_segment [L4]  id_keys=(segment_id)\n     reading=[packet_loss,probe_success,retrans_segs]  event=[link_flapping,mtu_changed,rekey_failed,tunnel_down]\n     - A network/subnet boundary (VLAN/CIDR) Hosts CONNECTS_TO — the transport family — use fo...\n  proxy [L4]  id_keys=(proxy_id)\n     event=[config_reloaded,connection_pool_exhausted,mtls_handshake_failed,upstream_timeout]\n     - A reverse/forward/sidecar/egress proxy (Envoy/nginx/HAProxy) — the path-device family s...\n  route [L4]  id_keys=(route_id)\n     event=[rule_changed]\n     - A single routing rule (path/host match) owned by a LoadBalancer/Dns — not the LB resour...\n  waf [L4]  id_keys=(waf_id)\n     event=[block_spike,rule_disabled,rule_set_updated]\n     - A web application firewall (L7 app-layer request filtering) — the policy family sibling...\n  build_artifact [L5]  id_keys=(digest)\n     event=[built,promoted]\n     - An immutable built artifact identified by digest, BUILT_FROM a CodeCommit and wrapped R...\n  certificate [L5]  id_keys=(cert_id)\n     state=[days_to_expiry]  event=[expired,issued,renewed]\n     - A TLS/cert credential (R-G6, change-adjacent-but-not-in-CMDB) whose `expired` event pow...\n  change_event [L5]  id_keys=(change_id)\n     property=[diff_summary,files_changed,lines_added,lines_deleted]  event=[closed,implemented,opened]\n     - A first-class ServiceNow-style change record (deploy/config/infra/db-migration) — essen...\n  code_commit [L5]  id_keys=(sha)\n     property=[blame_line,diff_summary,files_changed,lines_added,lines_deleted]\n     - An immutable commit (identity = sha) — the terminal node a blame/diff join resolves a C...\n  external_service [L5]  id_keys=(service_name)\n     reading=[availability,error_rate,latency_p99,request_rate]  event=[outage_resolved,outage_started]\n     - A third-party/SaaS dependency outside CMDB (R-G6) — a Service DEPENDS_ON it, or CALLS i...\n  feature_flag [L5]  id_keys=(flag_key,env)\n     state=[enabled,rollout_percentage]  event=[flipped]\n     - A flag whose `flipped` event (R-G6) is a change usually invisible to CMDB/git — a commo...\n  pull_request [L5]  id_keys=(repo,pr_id)\n     event=[closed,merged,opened]\n     - The review/merge record for one or more CodeCommits — use when the fixture surfaces PR ...\n  release [L5]  id_keys=(release_id)\n     event=[released,rolled_back]\n     - A named, deployable version wrapping a BuildArtifact, DEPLOYED_AS a running Deployment/...\n  alert [L6]  id_keys=(alert_id)\n     event=[ack,fired,flapping,re_fired,resolved]\n     - A monitoring-rule firing (Prometheus/AppD), FIRED_ON the entity it concerns\n  anomaly [L6]  id_keys=(anomaly_id)\n     state=[onset_value,severity_score]  event=[cleared,detected]\n     - THE canonical symptom node (R-G4) — FRAME's output, carrying the onset fact + AFFECTS->...\n  business_transaction [L6]  id_keys=(service_name,bt_name)\n     reading=[art_p95,calls_per_min,delta_vs_baseline,errors_per_min]  span=[trace]  event=[trace_captured]\n     - An AppDynamics business transaction — a named user-facing operation with its own RT/EPM...\n  error_signature [L6]  id_keys=(signature_hash)\n     property=[last_seen]  reading=[count]\n     - A deduplicated recurring error/exception pattern EMITTED by a Service/Pod (Splunk searc...\n  hypothesis [L6]  id_keys=(hid)\n     event=[confirmed,created,refuted,superseded]\n     - The graph-node projection of a hypothesis store Hypothesis record (see domain/hypothesi...\n  incident [L6]  id_keys=(incident_id)\n     event=[declared,mitigated,resolved]\n     - The ServiceNow-style incident record wrapping the investigation; AFFECTS points from it...\n  generic_ci [signal]  id_keys=(ci_id)\n     (peripheral — no cataloged predicates)\n     - The single escape hatch (mirrors ServiceNow base `cmdb_ci`) for any CI whose shape does...\n\n## EDGE TYPES  (legal (src_type -> dst_type) pairs; an illegal triple is REJECTED)\n##   AIRLOCK: `generic_ci` may stand in for either end of a STRUCTURAL edge (depends_on, calls,\n##   runs_on, ...) when its other end is legal there — the edge lands provisional at reduced\n##   confidence, origin=discovered. A generic_ci may also be NAMED A CAUSE via caused_by.\n  affects: anomaly->service; anomaly->api_endpoint; anomaly->database; anomaly->host; anomaly->business_transaction  (+4 more legal pairs)\n  built_from: build_artifact->code_commit; release->build_artifact\n  calls: service->service; service->api_endpoint; api_endpoint->service; component->service; service->external_service  (+2 more legal pairs)\n  caused_by: hypothesis->change_event; hypothesis->code_commit; hypothesis->certificate; hypothesis->feature_flag; hypothesis->firewall_rule  (+33 more legal pairs)  <requires confidence_level+evidence>\n  changed_by: service->change_event; database->change_event; host->change_event; deployment->change_event; firewall_rule->change_event  (+10 more legal pairs)\n  connects_to: host->network_segment; service->network_segment; load_balancer->network_segment; proxy->network_segment; api_gateway->network_segment  (+1 more legal pairs)\n  consumes_from: service->message_queue; batch_job->message_queue; component->message_queue\n  contains: namespace->pod; namespace->deployment; namespace->replicaset; namespace->config_item; cluster->namespace  (+1 more legal pairs)\n  correlated_with: anomaly->change_event; anomaly->alert; anomaly->anomaly; service->service; hypothesis->hypothesis  <requires confidence_level+evidence>\n  depends_on: service->service; service->database; service->message_queue; service->cache; service->external_service  (+9 more legal pairs)\n  deployed_as: release->deployment; release->pod; build_artifact->deployment; build_artifact->pod; deployment->release\n  deployed_to: deployment->namespace; deployment->cluster; release->namespace; release->cluster\n  emitted: service->error_signature; pod->error_signature; component->error_signature; container->error_signature; api_endpoint->error_signature\n  exposes: service->api_endpoint; deployment->api_endpoint; load_balancer->route; api_gateway->api_endpoint; api_gateway->route\n  fired_on: alert->service; alert->api_endpoint; alert->host; alert->database; alert->message_queue  (+9 more legal pairs)\n  hosted_on: host->cluster; database->host; message_queue->host; cache->host; load_balancer->host  (+1 more legal pairs)\n  impacts: change_event->service; change_event->database; change_event->api_endpoint; hypothesis->service; anomaly->business_transaction  <requires confidence_level+evidence>\n  instance_of: pod->deployment; replicaset->deployment; container->pod\n  introduced_by: change_event->code_commit; change_event->release; change_event->pull_request; release->code_commit\n  member_of: host->cluster; pod->namespace; service->team; component->service\n  owns: team->service; team->application; team->component; application->service\n  participated_in: service->business_transaction; api_endpoint->business_transaction; external_service->business_transaction; component->business_transaction; service->incident  (+5 more legal pairs)\n  produces_to: service->message_queue; batch_job->message_queue; component->message_queue\n  reads_from: service->database; service->cache; service->schema; component->database; component->cache\n  realizes: pod->replicaset; replicaset->deployment; pod->deployment\n  recurrence_of: incident->incident  <requires confidence_level+evidence>\n  refutes: application->hypothesis; service->hypothesis; component->hypothesis; api_endpoint->hypothesis; team->hypothesis  (+37 more legal pairs)  <requires confidence_level+evidence>\n  released_as: build_artifact->release\n  remediated_by: hypothesis->change_event; hypothesis->release; hypothesis->config_item; hypothesis->feature_flag; hypothesis->firewall_rule  (+1 more legal pairs)\n  routes_to: load_balancer->service; route->service; route->api_endpoint; dns->load_balancer; dns->cdn  (+12 more legal pairs)\n  runs_on: pod->host; container->host; process->host; batch_job->host\n  runs_version: deployment->release; pod->release; deployment->build_artifact; pod->build_artifact\n  secured_by: service->firewall_rule; network_segment->firewall_rule; route->firewall_rule; load_balancer->firewall_rule; database->firewall_rule  (+11 more legal pairs)\n  similar_to: incident->incident  <requires confidence_level+evidence>\n  supports: application->hypothesis; service->hypothesis; component->hypothesis; api_endpoint->hypothesis; team->hypothesis  (+37 more legal pairs)  <requires confidence_level+evidence>\n  triggered_by: incident->alert; anomaly->alert; incident->anomaly\n  writes_to: service->database; service->cache; service->schema; component->database; batch_job->database  (+1 more legal pairs)\n\n## NODE-ID CONVENTION (how to reference a node in a fact/edge/hypothesis)\n  id = \"<type>:\" + the node's identity_key values, slugged (lowercased, spaces/'/'->'-'),\n       joined by \"|\".  e.g. change_event with change_id=\"CHG-9\" -> \"change_event:chg-9\";\n       service with service_name=\"orders-api\", env=\"prod\" -> \"service:orders-api|prod\";\n       code_commit with sha=\"abc123\" -> \"code_commit:abc123\".\n  ALWAYS copy an exact id verbatim from the CURRENT GRAPH slice when the node already exists.\n\n## QUERY GRAMMAR — the DESK (pushed) + REACHING for more\n  Your DESK each turn is the FOCUS SLICE (pre-tiered: focus + cause-path + suspects in full, the\n  frontier to expand along, healthy nodes collapsed to a count) + the ranked hypotheses + the\n  engine-computed GRAPH PROJECTIONS. REASON over them; what the engine reaches for lands on the desk:\n    - state as-of-T   — the STATE tile TRUE at an instant (a version/image/severity AT onset, not now)\n    - metric summary  — a READING summarised over a window (through the metric_query handle)\n    - spans of a node — the SPAN datums it participates in, span_phase ALWAYS shown; a span whose\n                        interval CONTAINS onset IS the RCA overlap join (change window / outage / rollout)\n    - change-trail    — the STATE supersede-chain + the change-index (events, spans, change_events,\n                        AND every STATE version-boundary — so a silent bump is never missed)\n  You EXPAND over the OBSERVED spine; you only READ the derived causal/evidence layer as the slice\n  renders it (a topology query never drags in hypotheses).\n\n## PHASES (you are driving ONE phase per turn; the engine routes on your verdict)\n  frame: Normalize the signal: fix scope/severity/onset, seed the symptom (Anomaly) + subject + topology + candidate changes, and scope the impact.\n     allowed_intents (abstract action budget): ingest_alert, query_change_log, seed_graph, get_dependencies, assess_impact, list_dependencies\n     produces_required: ['nodes_touched', 'facts_added']\n     GATE (to ADVANCE or DONE): min_facts>=1\n     routes: advance->investigate, repeat->frame\n  investigate: ONE loop — hypothesize ⇄ gather evidence ⇄ refute: generate causal explanations change-first, gather targeted evidence to confirm or refute the leader, rule out rivals.\n     allowed_intents (abstract action budget): enumerate_changes, propose_hypotheses, correlate_timeline, fetch_logs, fetch_metrics, fetch_traces, read_diff, blame, query_change_log\n     produces_required: ['facts_added', 'hypotheses_updated']\n     GATE (to ADVANCE or DONE): leading-hypothesis confidence>=0.8; a rival ruled out OR the leader challenged with refuting evidence\n     routes: advance->act, repeat->investigate, backtrack->investigate\n  act: Execute the chosen production-changing action through the human approval gate — early mitigation and remediation are the same gated machinery; success is an approved, executed, journaled action.\n     allowed_intents (abstract action budget): propose_fix, apply_mitigation, apply_remediation\n     produces_required: ['hypotheses_updated']\n     routes: advance->verify, repeat->act, backtrack->investigate\n  verify: Did the symptom clear and does the confirmed chain still hold?\n     allowed_intents (abstract action budget): recheck_symptom, confirm_chain\n     produces_required: ['facts_added']\n     GATE (to ADVANCE or DONE): an active 'cleared' event on the symptom node\n     routes: advance->close, backtrack->investigate\n  close: Postmortem: the confirmed causal chain + timeline, folded from the journal.\n     allowed_intents (abstract action budget): render_postmortem\n     produces_required: (none)\n     routes: (terminal)\n\nTotal: 43 node types, 37 edge types.\n\n## AVAILABLE TOOLS — grouped by capability. Emit the exact intent names in `calls`.\n# ROUTING: each capability names the id it 'queries by'. Resolve that id off the target\n#   CI — the incident's Service carries app_id / repo / k8s_workload / sys_id, resolved\n#   from the incident record — and pass it in the call params. Do NOT reuse the display\n#   name for a tool that queries by a different id (AppD queries by app_id, git by repo,\n#   the platform by k8s_workload).\n  appd — Application topology, traces, and the JDBC/HTTP exit-call boundary · queries by `app_id`\n      intents: bt_health  fetch_traces  flowmap  get_snapshots  healthrule_violations\n  artifactory — Build → artifact → promotion lineage · queries by `repo`\n      intents: aql_search  get_artifact_by_digest  get_build  list_promotions\n  bigpanda — Event correlation — collapses an alert storm into one incident · queries by `incident_id`\n      intents: get_correlated_incident  get_flapping_signals  list_correlated_alerts\n  cmdb — The declared dependency topology and CI identity · queries by `service_name`\n      intents: find_ci_by_attr  get_ci_class  get_dependencies  impact_analysis  seed_graph\n  git — Diffs, blame, and pull-request context for a change · queries by `repo`\n      intents: blame  diff_range  get_commit  get_pr_for_commit  read_diff\n  ocp — Kubernetes / OpenShift rollout, pod, and event state · queries by `k8s_workload`\n      intents: events  pod_logs  pod_status  rollout_status\n  prometheus — Time-series metrics (RED/USE) and firing alerts · queries by `service_name`\n      intents: active_alerts  fetch_metrics  instant_query  range_query\n  servicenow — The incident record, its changes, related incidents, and the affected CI identity · queries by `incident_id`\n      intents: assess_impact  find_recent_changes  get_ci  get_incident  list_related_incidents  query_change_log\n  splunk — Logs, error signatures, and firewall-deny records · queries by `service_name`\n      intents: error_signature_topk  fetch_logs  search_errors  search_fw_denies  transaction_trace\n  ocp [WRITE — human-gated] — Kubernetes / OpenShift rollout, pod, and event state · queries by `k8s_workload`\n      intents: ocp__restart\n  remediation [WRITE — human-gated] — Apply a proposed, reversible remediation (human-gated) · queries by `service_name`\n      intents: apply_remediation\n  servicenow [WRITE — human-gated] — The incident record, its changes, related incidents, and the affected CI identity · queries by `incident_id`\n      intents: ingest_alert\n\n# TOOLS WIRED FOR THIS INCIDENT (ONLY these return data; any other\n# tool resolves but returns EMPTY — do not waste calls on them):\n#   active_alerts, assess_impact, blame, diff_range, error_signature_topk, fetch_logs, fetch_metrics, find_ci_by_attr, find_recent_changes, get_ci, get_ci_class, get_commit, get_dependencies, get_incident, get_pr_for_commit, impact_analysis, ingest_alert, instant_query, list_related_incidents, query_change_log, range_query, read_diff, search_errors, search_fw_denies, seed_graph, transaction_trace\n\n# INCIDENT\nsubject: {'domain': 'app-incident', 'id': 'INC-4821', 'kind': 'incident'}\n\n# CURRENT PHASE: investigate\ngoal: ONE loop — hypothesize ⇄ gather evidence ⇄ refute: generate causal explanations change-first, gather targeted evidence to confirm or refute the leader, rule out rivals.\nallowed_intents this phase (ABSTRACT categories — fulfil them with the WIRED tools above, not by\n  emitting these words as tool names): ['enumerate_changes', 'propose_hypotheses', 'correlate_timeline', 'fetch_logs', 'fetch_metrics', 'fetch_traces', 'read_diff', 'blame', 'query_change_log']\nproduces_required (must be non-empty to advance): ['facts_added', 'hypotheses_updated']\nGATE to ADVANCE: leading confidence>=0.8; a rival refuted OR the leader challenged\n# TEMPORALLY-CORRELATED CHANGE EVENTS (engine-computed, clock-skew-tolerant; candidates for the change-first hypothesis):\n#   - implemented on change_event:chg-1 at 2026-07-19T13:47:00+00:00 (lead 1080.0s; preceded onset)\nPROGRESSION RULE: set verdict=advance as soon as this phase's produces_required + gate are\n  satisfied — do NOT loop re-gathering evidence. In INVESTIGATE, verdict=repeat continues the\n  hypothesize⇄evidence⇄refute loop (propose early, refute before advancing); \"stop the\n  bleeding NOW\" is not a phase — enter ACT early with a mitigation action when impact demands\n  it (every production-changing action, mitigation or remediation alike, is a human-gated ACT\n  action). Only verdict=repeat when a REQUIRED output is genuinely still missing this phase.\n\n# CURRENT GRAPH — FOCUS SLICE (everything your prior tool calls have discovered, tiered by\n# relevance to the symptom: read the full cards for evidence, expand along the FRONTIER for\n# targeted evidence, and never re-propose a RULED OUT claim)\nFOCUS: anomaly:anom-inc-4821   total=6 nodes = 6 full + 0 frontier + 0 collapsed\nNODES (tiered by investigative relevance — full evidence cards):\n  [focus] anomaly:anom-inc-4821 (anomaly)  facts: onset_value=unknown_pending_incident_payloadsymptom\n  [suspect] change_event:chg-1 (change_event)  props: change_type=deployment, target_ref=payments-api, actor=dev-kco, ticket_id=CHG-1, short_description=Deploy payments-api v4.12.0 to prod (intl tax-calc), description=Standard release of payments-api v4.12.0 via Argo Rollouts. Bumps the shared taxcalc library to add intl VAT regions. Blue/green with a 10% canary, auto-promoted after the 5-minute analysis gate passed.\n  [suspect] code_commit:abc123 (code_commit)\n  [suspect] database:payments-ora (database)\n  [suspect] incident:inc-4821 (incident)  props: severity=2 - High, commander=sre-oncall, title=payments-api elevated 5xx errors, short_description=payments-api 5xx spiked to 40% ~13m after the v4.12.0 deploy, description=PagerDuty routed High5xxRate to SRE at 14:00 UTC. payments-api (prod, tier-1) is returning HTTP 5xx on ~40% of requests; throughput is holding but the error tail is dragging p99 to 4.2s while p50 stays flat. Onset is 13 minutes after release v4.12.0 rolled out at 13:47. Card auth + checkout capture are impacted; revenue-affecting. Investigating the deploy as the prime suspect., work_notes=[14:02] sre-oncall: High5xxRate paged; errors at 40% on payments-api. v4.12.0 shipped 13:47, ~13m before onset — change-first prime suspect.\n[14:26] sre-oncall: Splunk shows a NullPointerException in TaxCalculator, first seen at onset; payments-ora pool healthy (28%). Staging rollback to v4.11.3., caller_id=monitoring.alerting\n  [suspect] service:payments-api|prod (service)  props: env=prod, app_id=APM-PAYMEN, sys_id=sn_paymentsapi01, repo=payments-api, k8s_workload=prod/payments-api, owner=payments-platform@corp.example, version=v4.12.0\nEDGES:\n  introduced_by: change_event:chg-1 -> code_commit:abc123 [discovered]\n  affects: incident:inc-4821 -> service:payments-api|prod [discovered]\n  changed_by: service:payments-api|prod -> change_event:chg-1 [discovered]\n  depends_on: service:payments-api|prod -> database:payments-ora [declared]\n\n# RANKED HYPOTHESES (the hypothesis store so far — engine-earned confidence; `supporting`/\n# `refuting` are evidence COUNTS: a leader with refuting=0 has not been challenged yet)\n[]\n\nPlan this phase. Return ONLY the JSON object.","raw_response":"{\n  \"reasoning\": \"Change-first: CHG-1 deployed payments-api v4.12.0 (commit abc123, taxcalc bump) 13m before onset — prime suspect. Work notes already cite NullPointerException in TaxCalculator at onset and healthy DB pool, so lead with a code-defect hypothesis rooted at code_commit:abc123 and a rival rooted at database:payments-ora. Gather error signatures, commit diff/blame, and DB/service metrics in one pass to support the leader and refute the rival.\",\n  \"todos\": [\n    {\n      \"objective\": \"Propose leading code-defect hypothesis and DB rival\",\n      \"calls\": [],\n      \"ops\": [\n        {\n          \"op\": \"propose_hypothesis\",\n          \"hid\": \"h1\",\n          \"statement\": \"NullPointerException in TaxCalculator introduced by code_commit abc123 (taxcalc intl VAT bump) shipped via CHG-1/v4.12.0 causes payments-api 5xx spike\",\n          \"root_candidate\": \"code_commit:abc123\",\n          \"confidence_level\": \"med\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"op\": \"propose_hypothesis\",\n          \"hid\": \"h2\",\n          \"statement\": \"payments-ora database saturation or connection issue causes payments-api 5xx\",\n          \"root_candidate\": \"database:payments-ora\",\n          \"confidence_level\": \"low\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"objective\": \"Fetch error signatures and logs tying NPE to TaxCalculator at onset\",\n      \"calls\": [\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"error_signature_topk\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"service_name\": \"payments-api\",\n            \"env\": \"prod\",\n            \"since\": \"2026-07-19T13:45:00+00:00\",\n            \"until\": \"2026-07-19T14:30:00+00:00\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"search_errors\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"service_name\": \"payments-api\",\n            \"env\": \"prod\",\n            \"query\": \"NullPointerException TaxCalculator\",\n            \"since\": \"2026-07-19T13:45:00+00:00\",\n            \"until\": \"2026-07-19T14:30:00+00:00\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"fetch_logs\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"service_name\": \"payments-api\",\n            \"env\": \"prod\",\n            \"since\": \"2026-07-19T13:45:00+00:00\",\n            \"until\": \"2026-07-19T14:30:00+00:00\",\n            \"filter\": \"NullPointerException OR TaxCalculator\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"ops\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"objective\": \"Read commit diff and blame for taxcalc/TaxCalculator defect\",\n      \"calls\": [\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"get_commit\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"repo\": \"payments-api\",\n            \"sha\": \"abc123\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"read_diff\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"repo\": \"payments-api\",\n            \"sha\": \"abc123\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"blame\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"repo\": \"payments-api\",\n            \"sha\": \"abc123\",\n            \"path\": \"TaxCalculator\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"get_pr_for_commit\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"repo\": \"payments-api\",\n            \"sha\": \"abc123\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"ops\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"objective\": \"Fetch service RED and DB pool metrics to challenge DB rival\",\n      \"calls\": [\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"fetch_metrics\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"service_name\": \"payments-api\",\n            \"env\": \"prod\",\n            \"metrics\": [\"error_rate\", \"latency_p99\", \"latency_p50\", \"request_rate\"],\n            \"since\": \"2026-07-19T13:30:00+00:00\",\n            \"until\": \"2026-07-19T14:30:00+00:00\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"fetch_metrics\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"service_name\": \"payments-ora\",\n            \"env\": \"prod\",\n            \"metrics\": [\"conn_pool_util\", \"active_connections\", \"slow_query_rate\", \"replication_lag\"],\n            \"since\": \"2026-07-19T13:30:00+00:00\",\n            \"until\": \"2026-07-19T14:30:00+00:00\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"intent\": \"range_query\",\n          \"params\": {\n            \"query\": \"conn_pool_util{db_id=\\\"payments-ora\\\"}\",\n            \"start\": \"2026-07-19T13:30:00+00:00\",\n            \"end\": \"2026-07-19T14:30:00+00:00\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"ops\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Investigating CHG-1/v4.12.0 (commit abc123 taxcalc bump) as prime cause of payments-api 5xx. Proposing code NPE hypothesis vs DB rival; pulling error signatures, commit diff/blame, and service/DB metrics to confirm or refute.\",\n  \"verdict\": {\n    \"status\": \"repeat\",\n    \"confidence_level\": \"med\",\n    \"basis\": \"Hypotheses proposed and evidence gathering kicked off; need tool results (errors, diff, metrics) before supporting leader and refuting rival to satisfy the gate.\"\n  },\n  \"next_actions\": [\n    \"Inspect error_signature and log evidence for TaxCalculator NPE first_seen at onset\",\n    \"Inspect commit diff/blame for null-deref in taxcalc path\",\n    \"Confirm DB pool healthy to refute h2\",\n    \"Update h1 to supported/high and h2 to refuted, then advance\"\n  ]\n}","tokens_in":10314,"tokens_out":1416,"latency_ms":24606.27,"n_todos":4},"observation":null,"decision":null,"available":null,"plan_calls":null,"plan_ops":null,"todos":null,"todo":null,"refs":{}}
